`write_transformed_embeddings` writes what a subject transform made of embeddings read with `load_embeddings`, row for row, as one file holding every recording, e.g. Euclidean-aligned tokens as `desc-baseEaCoralCh_tokenembeddings.nc`: it keeps the windows, recordings and channels of the source and adds the setting `Transform`, so the loader never mixes it with its source; `view="cov"` writes `RiemannAlign`'s tangent vectors.
